From d6bd65a09082658f7a782679083f0953d5816826 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenMCX <noreply@openmcx.invalid>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:22:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ims_auth: usable local IMS AKA vectors (av_mode=1), and HTTP
 Digest AKAv2-SHA-256

Kamailio 6.1.4 ims_auth with av_mode=1 (the S-CSCF makes the vectors from K,
OPc and AMF set by ims_auth_data_set(), Milenage TS 35.206) cannot complete an
IMS AKA registration (TS 33.203 clause 6.1, TS 24.229 clause 5.4.1.2):

1. new_auth_userdata() leaves the record (its SQN, expiry, hash) uninitialised.
2. The SQN went up by 1 over all 48 bits after the vector was made, so the
   first vector of a user carried SEQ 0 and only IND moved; now each vector
   gets a fresh SQN before it is made: SEQ + 1 and the next IND (5 bits)
   (TS 33.102 annex C.1.1.2, C.1.2).
3. With that, a resynchronisation sets the SQN to SQN_MS and the next vector
   has SEQ_MS + 1 instead of repeating SQN_MS.
4. MAC-S of AUTS is checked with the all-zero AMF (TS 33.102 clause 6.3.3),
   not the subscriber's AMF, and with the RAND decoded from the vector's
   base64 nonce (it took the first 16 characters of the base64 text).
6. ims_auth_hexbin() stored a byte whenever the accumulated value was odd
   ("r % 2") instead of after every second digit ("i % 2").
7. ims_auth_data_set() marked OPc as given when it was empty.
8. get_auth_vector() did not link a new local vector into an empty list and
   did not return its hash slot.
9. ims_auth_data_set() returned 0 on success, which ends the script.
10. Two challenges in a row could carry the same RAND; RAND now comes from
    getrandom() for every vector (TS 33.102 clause 6.3.2).

And (5) HTTP Digest AKAv2 with SHA-256, which TS 33.203 clause 6.1.1 requires
the S-CSCF to offer before AKAv1-MD5: with the new parameter aka_v2_sha256=1
the 401 carries a WWW-Authenticate with algorithm=AKAv2-SHA-256 and then the
AKAv1-MD5 one, for the same vector; the response is checked with the algorithm
the Authorization names (TS 24.229 clause 5.4.1.2.2 step 3 b): password
base64(HMAC-SHA-256(RES || IK || CK, "http-digest-akav2-password")) (RFC 4169
section 3) and the SHA-256 digest of RFC 7616 section 3.4.1. No
Authentication-Info is added for AKAv2-SHA-256.

The modified files carry a notice of the change (GPL-2.0 section 2(a)).
